1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:03,439
I used OpenAI Codex to help build and

2
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:06,480
revise the app, check calculations and

3
00:00:06,480 --> 00:00:09,599
sources, and draft documentation and

4
00:00:09,599 --> 00:00:12,639
recording guides. The analysis and

5
00:00:12,639 --> 00:00:15,280
decision are mine. This is an

6
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,279
educational project for a fictional

7
00:00:17,279 --> 00:00:19,680
university scholarship fund, not

8
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,240
investment advice.

9
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,320
My thinking changed from finding a

10
00:00:24,320 --> 00:00:27,439
portfolio that passes numerical rules to

11
00:00:27,439 --> 00:00:29,119
asking whether a committee could

12
00:00:29,119 --> 00:00:32,160
responsibly use the process.

13
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:34,800
The fund needs scholarship reserves and

14
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:37,280
a return objective, but meeting modeled

15
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,600
requirements does not establish that the

16
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,520
portfolio is suitable for live

17
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,680
investment.

18
00:00:43,680 --> 00:00:46,879
One AI assisted output I checked was the

19
00:00:46,879 --> 00:00:49,760
model's response to higher costs. With

20
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,559
AI off, I predicted that raising annual

21
00:00:52,559 --> 00:00:56,480
costs from 25 to 35 basis points would

22
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:00,719
shift the paper portfolio from 75% SGOV

23
00:01:00,719 --> 00:01:03,920
and 25% ACWI

24
00:01:03,920 --> 00:01:07,680
to 70 and 30.

25
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:10,479
My prediction was committed before the

26
00:01:10,479 --> 00:01:14,280
changed input run.

27
00:01:18,560 --> 00:01:21,200
The prediction matched. The original

28
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,000
model's estimated net return moved from

29
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:25,600
5.51

30
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:28,400
to 5.83%.

31
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,000
While volatility increased from 3.81

32
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,400
to 4.54%.

33
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:39,119
Higher fees did not improve returns.

34
00:01:39,119 --> 00:01:41,600
Holding the original weights fixed would

35
00:01:41,600 --> 00:01:45,119
have lowered net return to 5.41%

36
00:01:45,119 --> 00:01:49,119
below the 5.5% objective.

37
00:01:49,119 --> 00:01:51,520
The model selected more equity exposure

38
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:53,759
to clear that hurdle, accepting more

39
00:01:53,759 --> 00:01:56,960
risk. A later review identified two

40
00:01:56,960 --> 00:01:59,840
weaknesses. No enforced numerical risk

41
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:01,680
ceiling and insufficient archived

42
00:02:01,680 --> 00:02:04,159
evidence for the original signal. I

43
00:02:04,159 --> 00:02:07,280
added a proposed 6% volatility ceiling

44
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:09,200
and replace the signal with dated

45
00:02:09,200 --> 00:02:13,479
Federal Reserve policy evidence.

46
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,560
These revisions changed the current

47
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:21,440
estimates to 5.57% at baseline and 5.89%

48
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:24,400
at higher costs. Those are revised model

49
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,959
results. My original prediction and

50
00:02:26,959 --> 00:02:30,000
experiment remain preserved separately.

51
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,080
So the later improvements do not rewrite

52
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:33,840
the evidence of what I predicted and

53
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,599
observed.

54
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:38,400
My recommendation remains a paper pilot

55
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,760
with zero live allocation. The 6%

56
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:44,400
ceiling is a research proposal, not an

57
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:46,480
approved client policy or a guarantee

58
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,480
against losses.

59
00:02:48,480 --> 00:02:51,200
Checking AI means testing outputs,

60
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:53,360
explaining changes, and letting

61
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:55,519
unresolved limitations constrain the

62
00:02:55,519 --> 00:02:58,080
decision.
